        Hint: '(He/she) is '
      meaning: "Similarly to \u3060, \u3067\u3059 is an auxiliary verb that is an
        expression of determination or assertion. It states that something 'is' a
        certain way. \u3067\u3059 is considered to be the polite variation of \u3060.
        Keep in mind though that although their roles are similar, both \u3060 and
        \u3067\u3059 are standalone structures."
